# Docs screenshots

When creating or updating a study README under `Docs/NN-*/README.md`:

1. **Take real screenshots** of the running app (local Vite / preview). Do not invent, AI-generate, or placeholder images.
2. Save them under that study’s `Images/` folder (create it if needed), using short kebab-case names (e.g. `ornament-branching.png`).
3. Embed them in the README next to the section they illustrate, following the pattern in `Docs/10-lsystems-lod/README.md`:

```markdown
![Short title](Images/filename.png)

*One-line caption: mode, preset, and what to notice.*
```

4. Prefer a few strong shots over many: each major mode / family / typology that the text describes should have at least one supporting image when the UI exists.
5. If the app cannot be opened, say so in the README and do not fabricate images.
